{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.AveragedLetterSpectrum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AveragedLetterSpectrum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.CharZero.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.second_parameter_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.second_parameter_forced","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AveragedLetterSpectrum.lean#L110-L124","doc":"**The second parameter is forced.**  If a scaled generator `c·T₀`, with `T₀`\nsatisfying `(T₀ − Q)(T₀ + Q⁻¹) = 0` so that `c·T₀` has eigenvalues `cQ` and\n`−cQ⁻¹`, is to carry the averaged letter's spectrum `±t`, then `Q² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.hecke_eigenvalues_not_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.hecke_eigenvalues_not_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AveragedLetterSpectrum.lean#L99-L107","doc":"A braid generator is **not** of this form: its eigenvalues `q` and `−q⁻¹` are\nnegatives of one another only when `q² = 1`.  This is precisely what the averaged\nletter gives up in exchange for being an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.averagedOn_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.averagedOn_sq","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AveragedLetterSpectrum.lean#L90-L96","doc":"**The averaged letter squares to the scalar `([2]_q/2)²`** on each Hecke\neigenvalue — \"it is a scaled involution\", in eigenvalue form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.averagedOn_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.averagedOn_neg","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AveragedLetterSpectrum.lean#L81-L88","doc":"On the `−q⁻¹` eigenvalue it takes `−[2]_q/2`.  With the previous lemma this\nis the whole point: the two values are **negatives of one another**, so the\naveraged letter is `[2]_q/2` times an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.averagedOn_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.averagedOn_pos","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AveragedLetterSpectrum.lean#L74-L79","doc":"On the `+q` eigenvalue the averaged letter takes the value `[2]_q/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.averagedOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.averagedOn","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AveragedLetterSpectrum.lean#L69-L72","doc":"The averaged letter `(σ + σ⁻¹)/2 = σ − h/2`, evaluated on an eigenvalue of\n`σ`.  `CharZero` is genuinely needed: the halving is not available in\ncharacteristic two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.qTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.qTwo","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AveragedLetterSpectrum.lean#L66-L67","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.heckeH","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AveragedLetterSpectrum.lean#L63-L64","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹`, the Hecke deformation parameter. ","signatureChunk":0}]}